  concept: 'Authored objective: Complete 148 training routes and 46 vias.

    Authored
    requirement: Verify continuity on the ten-layer PFX15-EDU-1 training circuit.

    General
    teaching principle: PCB acceptance depends on the authored footprints, nets,
    layers, clearances and route constraints; visual appearance alone is insufficient.

    Only
    fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A multilayer road map helps visualize routing, but electrical continuity
    and constraints still require checks.
